course: dictionary
lesson: 9687
title: Sufficient: just enough
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Sufficient» means enough, as much as is needed for a purpose. It is a formal word, so you will meet it in letters, science and exams. Look at the purpose: «Is 20 pounds sufficient to buy...?» asks whether 20 pounds is enough for what you want to buy.
explain: To check if something is sufficient, compare what is needed with what you have. In «sufficient water», you ask: is there enough water for the job? In «sufficient evidence», you ask: is there enough proof to show that something is true? Try swapping in the word "enough" to see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases use sufficient with a purpose. «Sufficient for» and «sufficient to» are followed by what the amount is for. «Self-sufficient» is a useful one: it means able to look after yourself.
fact: «Sufficient» is an adjective. The adverb is «sufficiently» and the noun is «sufficiency».
fact: «Sufficient» means enough, as much as is needed for a purpose.
fact: «Self-sufficient» means able to look after yourself.
fact: «Sufficient» is on the Years 5–6 spelling list in England, so it is worth learning to spell it correctly.
fact: Formal writing, such as a polite letter, often uses words like «sufficient», «sincerely» and «suggest».
exercise: «There was sufficient water for everyone on the hike.» What does sufficient mean here? | *Enough for what was needed | Too little to drink | Hot and steamy | Dirty and muddy
exercise: Which phrase means able to look after yourself? | Yours sincerely | sufficient water | *self-sufficient | sincerely
exercise: Is 20 pounds sufficient to buy a book that costs 15 pounds? | *Yes, 20 pounds is enough | It depends on the colour of the book | Only if the book is free | No, 20 pounds is never enough
test: Which sentence uses sufficient correctly? | *There was sufficient light to read by | The sufficient dog barked loudly | We sufficient ran home | Sufficient the sky was blue
test: Which word is the noun? | sufficiently | sincerely | *sufficiency | sufficient
exam: Ali says «sufficient» is a dull word. Why is it useful to know it? | It means exactly the same as sad | It means very large | It is only used by farmers | *It is common in formal letters and exams
